 ### Visits
 
-<a id="req-vis-001"></a><a id="req-vis-002"></a>
+<a id="req-vis-001"></a><a id="req-vis-002"></a><a id="req-vis-010"></a>
 
 A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a short description of what it is for `[REQ-VIS-001]`. When booking, the pet's earlier visits are shown alongside, so whoever is booking can see what has already been done `[REQ-VIS-002]`.
 
+Bookings are made by hand and go wrong: the visit lands on the wrong pet, or on the wrong day. Staff correct that from the owner's record, where every pet's visits are already listed. Each upcoming visit — one whose visit date is today or a later day — offers a cancel action there, and cancelling takes the visit off the pet's record outright, leaving the record as though the visit had never been booked. A visit whose date has passed is history and offers no cancel action `[REQ-VIS-010]` (requested 2026-08-05).
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a pet, when a description and a date later than today are supplied, then the visit is recorded and the booking is confirmed.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a blank description, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the description is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the date is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-002]` given a pet with earlier visits, when a new visit is being booked, then those earlier visits are shown with their dates and descriptions.
+- `[REQ-VIS-010]` given a pet with a visit dated today or later, when the owner's record is opened, then a cancel action is offered beside that visit.
+- `[REQ-VIS-010]` given a pet with a visit dated before today, when the owner's record is opened, then no cancel action is offered beside that visit.
+- `[REQ-VIS-010]` given an upcoming visit, when it is cancelled, then the owner's record is shown again and that visit is no longer on the pet's record.
+- `[REQ-VIS-010]` given an owner with several pets and several visits, when one visit is cancelled, then every other visit of every pet is unchanged.
+- `[REQ-VIS-010]` given a cancel request for a visit dated before today, when it is submitted, then it is refused and the visit remains on the record.
+- `[REQ-VIS-010]` given a cancel request naming a visit that is not on the named pet's record, when it is submitted, then it is refused and nothing is removed.
+- `[REQ-VIS-010]` given a reader using a supported language, when the owner's record is opened, then the cancel action is worded in that language.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. Booking a visit for a pet that does not belong to the named owner is refused.
 2. The date offered by default is the earliest date that would be accepted.
+3. A visit dated today is cancellable, although a visit dated today cannot be booked. The record carries no time of day, so the system cannot know whether today's visit has happened, and the day of the visit is when a wrong-day booking is most often noticed.
+4. Cancelling the same visit twice — a stale page, a double submission — is refused the second time, because the visit is no longer on the pet's record.
+5. After a cancellation the pet's record is indistinguishable from one where the visit was never booked; nothing marks that a visit was cancelled (NG-10).
+
